    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Appropriations",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7428\n\nSPONSOR: FELDER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act making an appropriation to pay Jennifer Sima-\nnowitz, widow of the late Michael A. Simanowitz, member of the Assembly\nfrom the 27th assembly district, the balance due of his unpaid annual\ncompensation for a portion of the year 2017\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize payment of unpaid annual compensation to Jennifer Simanow-\nitz, widow of Michael A. Simanowitz, member of the Assembly from the\n27th assembly district.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one authorizes the sum of twenty-nine thousand five hundred\nthirty-eight dollars and forty-two cents ($29,538.42) to be appropriated\nout of general fund for payment to Jennifer Simanowitz, the widow of the\nlate Michael A. Simanowitz, member of the Assembly, who died on the\nsecond day of September, 2017, for the balance due of the unpaid annual\ncompensation which would have been earned by him had he continued to\nlive and serve as such member until the end of 2017. Section two is the\neffective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIt has been the tradition of the Legislature to pay widows or widowers\nthe unpaid salaries of the Spouses who die while they are members of the\nLegislature.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\n$29,538.42.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
